   },
   "text": "Population Cycles in a Dimensionless Predator-Prey System"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i1",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44607,
    "y": 0.22284,
    "w": 0.10787,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "B. Fieldwork"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i2",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44393,
    "y": 0.25372,
    "w": 0.11215,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "October 2026"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i3",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.46419,
    "y": 0.3066,
    "w": 0.07163,
    "h": 0.01258
   },
   "text": "Abstract"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i4",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.17398,
    "y": 0.3305,
    "w": 0.65206,
    "h": 0.05786
   },
   "text": "We examine the classical predator-prey interaction after rescaling to dimensionless variables, where the prey density is x and the predator density is y. The oscillation period and the phase lag between the two populations follow from the trajectory starting at the field-observed initial state."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i5",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.41474,
    "w": 0.33467,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "1 The dimensionless system"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i6",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.449,
    "w": 0.31886,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "text": "In dimensionless form the dynamics read"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i7",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.45478,
    "y": 0.47995,
    "w": 0.41581,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { x } = x - x y ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i8",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.45559,
    "y": 0.51089,
    "w": 0.415,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { y } = x y - y ."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i9",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.55082,
    "w": 0.24557,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "2 Field observations"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i10",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.58508,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.04799
   },
   "text": "The pond was seeded from the survey counts, giving the initial state x(0) = 2 and y(0) = 0.5. All trajectories reported below start from these values; the predator peak follows the prey peak by roughly a quarter cycle, as expected for this system."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i11",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.65921,
    "w": 0.15696,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "3 Discussion"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i12",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.69347,
    "w": 0.74119,
    "h": 0.03088
   },
   "text": "Small perturbations of the initial state preserve the closed orbits, which is the stabilising property exploited by the field census design."
  }
 ]
}